{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KpGJ74QWD5bXy12ngHZmPE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier definition they provided. Let me identify the planned experiments:\n\n1. **diagnostic-rerepair** (planned) - Downstream proof-of-concept: give repair agent per-test failure predictions vs no per-test info, compare resolve rate on 200 instances.\n\n2. **swebench-pertest-data** (planned) - Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test labels.\n\nAnd from the what_if section:\n3. **re-repair-phase1-instruct** - Re-repair experiment with fixed confounds\n\n\nI'm also checking the running experiments since they're relevant to the \"best\" tier predictions, which depends on DeepSeek repo results. Looking back at the tier definition, I need to understand what \"best\" means: significant positive results from re-repair phase 1 combined with clear DeepSeek repo support for design space characterization.\n\nThe core assumptions break down into two possible paths based on DeepSeek's performance. Path B assumes CWM has a formulation advantage that's model-dependent, while Path A shows a consistent but smaller advantage for CLS over CWM. I'm tracking specific metric ranges to validate these assumptions: the re-repair resolve improvement should be 10-18 percentage points, the oracle versus diagnostic gap should be 5-12 points, and DeepSeek's accuracy metrics need to fall within expected ranges for both CLS and CWM approaches.\n\nLooking at the experiment pipeline, I have the diagnostic re-repair setup ready, the data preparation step queued, and the actual re-repair phase one experiment designed. For DeepSeek specifically, I'm running parallel repo-level experiments across CWM and CLS variants with different seeds, and I already have function-level results showing CLS achieving 86% accuracy, which gives me a baseline to compare against.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the detailed performance metrics across all the variants—the function-level accuracies for both CWM and CLS models with and without the seed modifications, the trajectory-based repo results at different context lengths, and the Qwen checkpoint performance across validation and test sets.\n\nLooking at the patterns, I'm identifying what constitutes the \"best\" tier for DeepSeek repo-level work: either CWM unparseable rates below 20% (which would support the model-contingent advantage path), or rates between 30-50% paired with CLS outperforming CWM by 5-10 percentage points. Since the function-level CWM already achieves 0% unparseable, it makes sense to expect similar low unparseable rates at the repo level—DeepSeek's tokenizer appears well-suited for structured outputs.\n\nNow I'm laying out the planned experiments to test: diagnostic re-repair, swebench per-test data variants, and the re-repair phase 1 instruct approach.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33520,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33520},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9104f1-6ad4-4926-a0cf-0c7bcf3666b7","uuid":"334d2f88-97e9-4824-b635-2eeb36a2d4a4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KpGJ74QWD5bXy12ngHZmPE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: \"原始 design space characterization framing 完全成立，且新增 downstream utility section 作为第四贡献。Claims: (1) formulation equivalence at func-level, (2) complexity-dependent divergence is model-contingent (Qwen CWM collapse vs DeepSeek CWM functional), (3) diagnostic granularity at no accuracy cost, (4) diagnostic info enables targeted re-repair (+10-15pp resolve rate). 论文从 empirical characterization 升级为 characterization + actionable downstream benefit。EMNLP Main 有力投稿。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # === DeepSeek Repo-Level (RUNNING) ===\n  - name: deepseek-cls-repo-v4\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA classification on SWE-bench repo-level data, seed 42, max_seq_len=8192\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 82.3\n      f1_macro: 78.5\n      f1_fail: 70.2\n      f1_pass: 86.8\n      precision_fail: 75.4\n      recall_fail: 65.7\n      precision_pass: 84.9\n      recall_pass: 88.8\n      unparseable_pct: 1.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 9.34\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 在 func-level CLS 达到 86.9%，repo-level 由于上下文更长、代码更复杂，预期下降约 4-5pp。Qwen3-4B repo CLS 在 ckpt-4600 test 上达到 83.63%，DeepSeek-8B 应在类似水平或略低（因为 DeepSeek LoRA 在 func-level 并未超过 Qwen CLS 太多）。DeepSeek tokenizer 产生的 unparseable 极低（func-level 为 0），repo-level 也应保持 <2%。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-Level CLS (seed 42) — Accuracy 82.3%, F1_macro 78.5%, gap vs majority +9.3pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix showing balanced precision/recall tradeoff, no severe bias toward pass or fail\"\n    analysis: \"DeepSeek CLS repo-level 表现与 Qwen CLS 8B (84.8% best ckpt) 相当，略低 2-3pp 可能因为 DeepSeek base model 对 Python 代码的 pre-training distribution 不同。关键是 unparseable 保持极低，确认 CLS formulation 在两个 model family 上都 robust。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cls-repo-s123\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CLS seed 123 replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 80.8\n      f1_macro: 76.9\n      f1_fail: 68.1\n      f1_pass: 85.7\n      unparseable_pct: 1.0\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 7.84\n    result_rationale: \"Seed variance 在 repo-level 约 ±1.5pp（参考 Qwen 4B ckpt 间差异）。Seed 123 可能略低于 seed 42，但仍显著高于 majority baseline。两个 seed 均值约 81.5% 确认 DeepSeek CLS repo-level 的可靠性。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CLS multi-seed — mean 81.6 ± 1.1%\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"两个 seed 结果一致性好（差异 <2pp），支持 CLS formulation 在 DeepSeek repo-level 的稳定性。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cwm-repo\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation, seed 42, max_new_tokens=1024, max_seq_len=8192\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 78.5\n      f1_macro: 72.3\n      f1_fail: 60.8\n      f1_pass: 83.8\n      unparseable_pct: 11.8\n      exact_match_rate: 52.3\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 5.54\n      gen_length_mean: 280\n      gen_length_median: 195\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek func-level CWM 0% unparseable，但 repo-level 输出更复杂（多测试结果、长 traceback），预期 unparseable 升至 10-15%。这远低于 Qwen 的 53-93%，证实 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific。Accuracy 因 unparseable 被判 fail 而下降，但 parseable subset 准确率应接近 func-level 的 85-87%。CLS-CWM gap 约 3-4pp，在 best tier 定义的 [-2, 10] 范围内。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM — Accuracy 78.5%, Unparseable 11.8% (vs Qwen 53-93%)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: CWM unparseable rate by model family — Qwen 54-93% vs DeepSeek 11.8%, demonstrating tokenizer-specific failure\"\n    analysis: \"核心发现：DeepSeek CWM 在 repo-level 的 unparseable 从 Qwen 的灾难性 53-93% 降至 11.8%，直接证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer/model-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。CLS 仍有 3-4pp 优势但差距大幅缩小，支持 Path B narrative：formulation advantage is model-contingent。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation seed 123 replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 76.9\n      f1_macro: 70.5\n      f1_fail: 58.3\n      f1_pass: 82.7\n      unparseable_pct: 14.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 3.94\n    result_rationale: \"Seed 123 CWM 可能 unparseable 略高（generation 的随机性更大），但仍保持 <20%。Accuracy 因 unparseable 上升而略降。两 seed 均值 unparseable 约 13%，远低于 Qwen 的 50%+ baseline。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM multi-seed — mean accuracy 77.7 ± 1.1%, mean unparseable 13.0 ± 1.7%\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"CWM 的 seed variance 略大于 CLS（generation 的 stochastic nature），但核心结论不变：DeepSeek CWM functional at repo-level。\"\n\n  # === Re-Repair Experiments (PLANNED) ===\n  - name: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n    plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n    description: \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct on 60 SWE-bench Verified instances. 5 conditions: A1 (minimal control), A2 (test-names-only), B (CLS-diagnostic predictions), C (oracle ground-truth diagnostic), D (random diagnostic). Docker-based resolve rate. pass@1 and pass@5 (temperature=0.7). Paired design across conditions.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 60\n      samples_per_condition: 5\n      # pass@1 resolve rates\n      A1_control_resolve_rate: 0.183\n      A2_test_names_resolve_rate: 0.217\n      B_cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.317\n      C_oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.400\n      D_random_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.150\n      # deltas\n      B_vs_A1_delta_pp: 13.3\n      B_vs_A2_delta_pp: 10.0\n      C_vs_B_delta_pp: 8.3\n      C_vs_A1_delta_pp: 21.7\n      D_vs_A1_delta_pp: -3.3\n      # pass@5 resolve rates\n      A1_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.283\n      B_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.433\n      C_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.533\n      # statistical\n      B_vs_A1_mcnemar_p: 0.031\n      C_vs_A1_mcnemar_p: 0.004\n      gradient_monotonic: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Best tier 要求 B vs A1 delta 在 [10, 18]pp 范围内，oracle vs CLS delta 在 [5, 12]pp。\n      \n      A1 (minimal control, ~18%): SWE-bench Verified 上 8B instruct 模型的 baseline resolve rate 大约在 15-22%（参考 SWE-agent + GPT-4 约 12%，但这里是 simpler prompt + smaller subset of easier instances）。\n      \n      A2 (test names, ~22%): 仅知道哪些 test 存在但不知道 pass/fail 状态，提供 minor structural guidance，提升 3-4pp。\n      \n      B (CLS diagnostic, ~32%): 模型预测的 per-test pass/fail 信息让 repair agent 能 focus on specific failures。即使预测有 ~12% error rate，fail_recall 93.6% 意味着绝大多数真实 failure 被正确标出。Agent 可以 target specific failing tests 而非盲目搜索。13pp 提升合理因为：(1) 搜索空间大幅缩小, (2) agent 可写 targeted fix 而非 shotgun approach, (3) 即使部分 FP/FN 存在，overall signal quality 足够 actionable。\n      \n      C (oracle, ~40%): Ground-truth per-test info 消除了 verifier 的 prediction noise。额外 8pp 提升来自：消除 FP（不再 fix 不需要 fix 的 test）和 FN（不遗漏真实 failures）。C-B gap 反映 verifier 预测质量的 ceiling。\n      \n      D (random, ~15%): 随机 per-test labels 反而 mislead agent，比 no-info 还差 3pp。确认 diagnostic info 的价值来自 signal quality 而非 mere presence of structured info。\n      \n      梯度 D < A1 < A2 < B < C 清晰成立，McNemar test p < 0.05 for B vs A1 on n=60。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Re-Repair Resolve Rates (pass@1, n=60)\n        Condition | Resolve Rate | Δ vs A1 | p-value\n        D (random diag) | 15.0% | -3.3pp | 0.62\n        A1 (no info) | 18.3% | — | —\n        A2 (test names) | 21.7% | +3.3pp | 0.41\n        B (CLS diag) | 31.7% | +13.3pp | 0.031*\n        C (oracle diag) | 40.0% | +21.7pp | 0.004**\n      - |\n        Table: Re-Repair pass@5 Comparison\n        A1: 28.3% → B: 43.3% → C: 53.3%\n        CLS-diagnostic nearly halves the gap between no-info and oracle\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with 95% CI error bars: resolve rate by condition. Clear monotonic gradient D < A1 < A2 < B < C.\"\n      - \"Paired instance analysis: heatmap showing which instances flip from unresolved→resolved with diagnostic info. Concentration in multi-test-failure instances.\"\n    analysis: |\n      Re-repair 结果强力支持 downstream utility claim。核心 insight：\n      1. CLS diagnostic info 即使有 ~12% error rate 仍提供 +13pp resolve rate 提升\n      2. 提升集中在 multi-test-failure instances（与 oracle-f2p-stratified 结果一致：T2+ instances 贡献 >80% of improvement）\n      3. 清晰梯度证明 diagnostic quality matters（random hurts, noisy-but-real helps, perfect helps most）\n      4. Oracle-CLS gap (8pp) 量化了 verifier 改进的剩余空间，motivating future work\n      \n      这直接回应 reviewer concern \"no downstream utility\"：per-test diagnostic 不仅在 accuracy 上 equivalent to trajectory-level，还 enables a concrete downstream application。\n\n  - name: swebench-pertest-data\n    plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test ground-truth labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances: 500\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_evaluations: 8000\n      successful_docker_runs: 7680\n      docker_failure_rate: 0.04\n      mean_tests_per_instance: 12.3\n      median_tests_per_instance: 8\n      f2p_distribution:\n        T1_pct: 45.2\n        T2_pct: 22.8\n        T3_5_pct: 18.6\n        T6plus_pct: 13.4\n      mean_resolve_rate_across_candidates: 0.31\n      total_per_test_labels: 94720\n      wall_time_hours: 18\n      parallelism: 16\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench Verified 有 500 个 curated instances。每个 instance 跑 16 个 repair candidate（来自不同 repair agent/model 的 patches）。Docker evaluation 的 failure rate 约 4%（timeout, dependency issues）。\n      \n      F2P test distribution 比 func-level dataset 更丰富（mean 12.3 vs func-level 的 2.3），因为 repo-level tests 涵盖更多 edge cases。T6+ 占 13.4% 意味着 per-test granularity 的优势在 repo-level 更大。\n      \n      这个 dataset 是 resource contribution：first large-scale per-test labeled dataset for SWE-bench。支撑 repo-level training 和 re-repair evaluation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\n        Instances: 500 | Candidates/instance: 16 | Total evaluations: 8000\n        Successful runs: 7680 (96%) | Total per-test labels: 94,720\n        Mean tests/instance: 12.3 | Median: 8\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of tests-per-instance distribution, showing long tail (some instances with 50+ tests)\"\n    analysis: \"Dataset 构建成功，为 repo-level experiments 和 re-repair evaluation 提供基础。F2P distribution 比 func-level 更重 tail（T6+ 13.4% vs 5.1%），预示 per-test advantage 在 repo-level 更显著。\"\n\n  - name: diagnostic-rerepair-pilot\n    plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n    description: \"Original planned experiment: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs no info on 200 instances. Superseded by re-repair-phase1-instruct design but kept for completeness.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 200\n      control_resolve_rate: 0.19\n      cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.33\n      delta_pp: 14.0\n      paired_t_p_value: 0.008\n      effect_size_cohens_d: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"在 200 instances 上 paired design 给出更强 statistical power。Delta 14pp 在 best tier [10,18] 范围内。Larger n 使得 p < 0.01 成为可能。Effect size medium (d=0.42) 反映 diagnostic info 是 useful-but-not-transformative intervention。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Larger sample 版本确认 re-repair-phase1-instruct 的发现，提供更强 statistical evidence。\"\n\n  # === Composite Analysis for Paper ===\n  - name: deepseek-repo-composite-analysis\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"Cross-model repo-level comparison: Qwen vs DeepSeek × CLS vs CWM. Design space characterization 的核心 table。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Qwen3-4B repo-level (from existing data)\n      qwen4b_cls_accuracy: 83.63\n      qwen4b_cwm_accuracy: 58.04\n      qwen4b_cwm_unparseable_pct: 53.7\n      qwen4b_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 25.59\n      # Qwen3-8B repo-level (from existing data)\n      qwen8b_cls_accuracy: 84.79\n      qwen8b_cwm_unparseable_pct: 93.0\n      # DeepSeek repo-level (predicted)\n      deepseek_cls_accuracy: 81.6\n      deepseek_cwm_accuracy: 77.7\n      deepseek_cwm_unparseable_pct: 13.0\n      deepseek_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 3.9\n      # DeepSeek func-level (from existing data)\n      deepseek_func_cls_accuracy: 86.85\n      deepseek_func_cwm_accuracy: 86.83\n      deepseek_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 0.02\n      # Qwen func-level (from existing data)\n      qwen_func_cls_accuracy: 88.41\n      qwen_func_cwm_accuracy: 87.19\n      qwen_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 1.22\n      # TRAJ comparison\n      deepseek_traj_repo_accuracy: 77.1\n      qwen_traj_repo_accuracy: 85.66\n    result_rationale: |\n      Design space characterization 的核心 evidence：\n      \n      Function-level: CLS ≈ CWM 在两个 model family 上都成立（gap < 1.5pp，TOST equivalence confirmed）。证明 formulation choice at low complexity 不重要。\n      \n      Repo-level divergence pattern:\n      - Qwen: CLS >> CWM (25pp gap)，因为 CWM unparseable 53-93%。Tokenizer 无法 handle structured multi-test output。\n      - DeepSeek: CLS > CWM (4pp gap)，CWM unparseable 仅 13%。Tokenizer 支持 structured generation。\n      \n      这是 Path B narrative：formulation advantage magnitude is model-contingent。CLS 仍有 consistent（小）优势，但 CWM 在合适的 tokenizer 下 functional。\n      \n      关键 insight：Qwen 的 CWM \"failure\" 不是因为 generation-based verification 不可行，而是因为其 tokenizer 在长结构化输出时 degenerate。DeepSeek 证明这不是 formulation-inherent limitation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Design Space — Accuracy by Formulation × Model × Complexity\n                    | Function-Level      | Repo-Level\n        Model       | CLS   | CWM  | Gap  | CLS   | CWM   | Gap   | CWM Unparse\n        Qwen3-4B    | 88.4  | 87.2 | +1.2 | 83.6  | 58.0  | +25.6 | 53.7%\n        Qwen3-8B    | 90.5  | 87.7 | +2.8 | 84.8  | —     | —     | 93.0%\n        DeepSeek-8B | 86.9  | 86.8 | +0.0 | 81.6  | 77.7  | +3.9  | 13.0%\n      - |\n        Table: Formulation Robustness Summary\n        Formulation | Func-Level (2 models) | Repo-Level (2 models)\n        CLS         | 86.9–90.5 (robust)    | 81.6–84.8 (robust)\n        CWM         | 86.8–87.7 (robust)    | 58.0–77.7 (fragile, model-dependent)\n        TRAJ        | 85.7–86.2             | 77.1–85.7 (variable)\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap: rows = model family (Qwen, DeepSeek), cols = complexity (func, repo). Cell color = CLS-CWM gap. Shows divergence only in top-right (Qwen × repo).\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: CWM unparseable rate (x) vs CLS-CWM accuracy gap (y). Strong positive correlation. Qwen repo as outlier, DeepSeek repo near origin.\"\n    analysis: |\n      Best tier narrative 完全成立：\n      1. Claim 1 (equivalence at func-level): ✓ 两个 model family 均 confirmed\n      2. Claim 2 (model-contingent divergence): ✓ DeepSeek CWM functional (13% unparse) vs Qwen CWM collapse (53-93%)\n      3. Claim 3 (diagnostic granularity): ✓ CLS per-test matches TRAJ accuracy while enabling re-repair\n      4. Claim 4 (downstream utility): ✓ +13pp resolve rate from CLS diagnostic info\n      \n      EMNLP Main 投稿强度：4 个 clean contributions，controlled comparison methodology，两个 model families 交叉验证，downstream application validated。唯一 limitation 是 repo-level sample size 较小（48 test instances per seed），但 multi-seed replication 部分弥补。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33520,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33520},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9104f1-6ad4-4926-a0cf-0c7bcf3666b7","uuid":"bf4d6a87-44d5-4e0d-8ac8-f5cc972c2be8"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":148463,"duration_api_ms":149818,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: \"原始 design space characterization framing 完全成立，且新增 downstream utility section 作为第四贡献。Claims: (1) formulation equivalence at func-level, (2) complexity-dependent divergence is model-contingent (Qwen CWM collapse vs DeepSeek CWM functional), (3) diagnostic granularity at no accuracy cost, (4) diagnostic info enables targeted re-repair (+10-15pp resolve rate). 论文从 empirical characterization 升级为 characterization + actionable downstream benefit。EMNLP Main 有力投稿。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # === DeepSeek Repo-Level (RUNNING) ===\n  - name: deepseek-cls-repo-v4\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA classification on SWE-bench repo-level data, seed 42, max_seq_len=8192\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 82.3\n      f1_macro: 78.5\n      f1_fail: 70.2\n      f1_pass: 86.8\n      precision_fail: 75.4\n      recall_fail: 65.7\n      precision_pass: 84.9\n      recall_pass: 88.8\n      unparseable_pct: 1.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 9.34\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-600\"\n      total_samples: 9784\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 在 func-level CLS 达到 86.9%，repo-level 由于上下文更长、代码更复杂，预期下降约 4-5pp。Qwen3-4B repo CLS 在 ckpt-4600 test 上达到 83.63%，DeepSeek-8B 应在类似水平或略低（因为 DeepSeek LoRA 在 func-level 并未超过 Qwen CLS 太多）。DeepSeek tokenizer 产生的 unparseable 极低（func-level 为 0），repo-level 也应保持 <2%。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo-Level CLS (seed 42) — Accuracy 82.3%, F1_macro 78.5%, gap vs majority +9.3pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix showing balanced precision/recall tradeoff, no severe bias toward pass or fail\"\n    analysis: \"DeepSeek CLS repo-level 表现与 Qwen CLS 8B (84.8% best ckpt) 相当，略低 2-3pp 可能因为 DeepSeek base model 对 Python 代码的 pre-training distribution 不同。关键是 unparseable 保持极低，确认 CLS formulation 在两个 model family 上都 robust。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cls-repo-s123\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CLS seed 123 replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 80.8\n      f1_macro: 76.9\n      f1_fail: 68.1\n      f1_pass: 85.7\n      unparseable_pct: 1.0\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 7.84\n    result_rationale: \"Seed variance 在 repo-level 约 ±1.5pp（参考 Qwen 4B ckpt 间差异）。Seed 123 可能略低于 seed 42，但仍显著高于 majority baseline。两个 seed 均值约 81.5% 确认 DeepSeek CLS repo-level 的可靠性。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CLS multi-seed — mean 81.6 ± 1.1%\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"两个 seed 结果一致性好（差异 <2pp），支持 CLS formulation 在 DeepSeek repo-level 的稳定性。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cwm-repo\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation, seed 42, max_new_tokens=1024, max_seq_len=8192\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 78.5\n      f1_macro: 72.3\n      f1_fail: 60.8\n      f1_pass: 83.8\n      unparseable_pct: 11.8\n      exact_match_rate: 52.3\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 5.54\n      gen_length_mean: 280\n      gen_length_median: 195\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek func-level CWM 0% unparseable，但 repo-level 输出更复杂（多测试结果、长 traceback），预期 unparseable 升至 10-15%。这远低于 Qwen 的 53-93%，证实 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific。Accuracy 因 unparseable 被判 fail 而下降，但 parseable subset 准确率应接近 func-level 的 85-87%。CLS-CWM gap 约 3-4pp，在 best tier 定义的 [-2, 10] 范围内。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM — Accuracy 78.5%, Unparseable 11.8% (vs Qwen 53-93%)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: CWM unparseable rate by model family — Qwen 54-93% vs DeepSeek 11.8%, demonstrating tokenizer-specific failure\"\n    analysis: \"核心发现：DeepSeek CWM 在 repo-level 的 unparseable 从 Qwen 的灾难性 53-93% 降至 11.8%，直接证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer/model-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。CLS 仍有 3-4pp 优势但差距大幅缩小，支持 Path B narrative：formulation advantage is model-contingent。\"\n\n  - name: deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"DeepSeek repo-level CWM generation seed 123 replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      test_accuracy: 76.9\n      f1_macro: 70.5\n      f1_fail: 58.3\n      f1_pass: 82.7\n      unparseable_pct: 14.2\n      majority_baseline: 72.96\n      gap_vs_majority_pp: 3.94\n    result_rationale: \"Seed 123 CWM 可能 unparseable 略高（generation 的随机性更大），但仍保持 <20%。Accuracy 因 unparseable 上升而略降。两 seed 均值 unparseable 约 13%，远低于 Qwen 的 50%+ baseline。\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: DeepSeek Repo CWM multi-seed — mean accuracy 77.7 ± 1.1%, mean unparseable 13.0 ± 1.7%\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"CWM 的 seed variance 略大于 CLS（generation 的 stochastic nature），但核心结论不变：DeepSeek CWM functional at repo-level。\"\n\n  # === Re-Repair Experiments (PLANNED) ===\n  - name: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n    plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n    description: \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct on 60 SWE-bench Verified instances. 5 conditions: A1 (minimal control), A2 (test-names-only), B (CLS-diagnostic predictions), C (oracle ground-truth diagnostic), D (random diagnostic). Docker-based resolve rate. pass@1 and pass@5 (temperature=0.7). Paired design across conditions.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 60\n      samples_per_condition: 5\n      # pass@1 resolve rates\n      A1_control_resolve_rate: 0.183\n      A2_test_names_resolve_rate: 0.217\n      B_cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.317\n      C_oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.400\n      D_random_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.150\n      # deltas\n      B_vs_A1_delta_pp: 13.3\n      B_vs_A2_delta_pp: 10.0\n      C_vs_B_delta_pp: 8.3\n      C_vs_A1_delta_pp: 21.7\n      D_vs_A1_delta_pp: -3.3\n      # pass@5 resolve rates\n      A1_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.283\n      B_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.433\n      C_pass5_resolve_rate: 0.533\n      # statistical\n      B_vs_A1_mcnemar_p: 0.031\n      C_vs_A1_mcnemar_p: 0.004\n      gradient_monotonic: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Best tier 要求 B vs A1 delta 在 [10, 18]pp 范围内，oracle vs CLS delta 在 [5, 12]pp。\n      \n      A1 (minimal control, ~18%): SWE-bench Verified 上 8B instruct 模型的 baseline resolve rate 大约在 15-22%（参考 SWE-agent + GPT-4 约 12%，但这里是 simpler prompt + smaller subset of easier instances）。\n      \n      A2 (test names, ~22%): 仅知道哪些 test 存在但不知道 pass/fail 状态，提供 minor structural guidance，提升 3-4pp。\n      \n      B (CLS diagnostic, ~32%): 模型预测的 per-test pass/fail 信息让 repair agent 能 focus on specific failures。即使预测有 ~12% error rate，fail_recall 93.6% 意味着绝大多数真实 failure 被正确标出。Agent 可以 target specific failing tests 而非盲目搜索。13pp 提升合理因为：(1) 搜索空间大幅缩小, (2) agent 可写 targeted fix 而非 shotgun approach, (3) 即使部分 FP/FN 存在，overall signal quality 足够 actionable。\n      \n      C (oracle, ~40%): Ground-truth per-test info 消除了 verifier 的 prediction noise。额外 8pp 提升来自：消除 FP（不再 fix 不需要 fix 的 test）和 FN（不遗漏真实 failures）。C-B gap 反映 verifier 预测质量的 ceiling。\n      \n      D (random, ~15%): 随机 per-test labels 反而 mislead agent，比 no-info 还差 3pp。确认 diagnostic info 的价值来自 signal quality 而非 mere presence of structured info。\n      \n      梯度 D < A1 < A2 < B < C 清晰成立，McNemar test p < 0.05 for B vs A1 on n=60。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Re-Repair Resolve Rates (pass@1, n=60)\n        Condition | Resolve Rate | Δ vs A1 | p-value\n        D (random diag) | 15.0% | -3.3pp | 0.62\n        A1 (no info) | 18.3% | — | —\n        A2 (test names) | 21.7% | +3.3pp | 0.41\n        B (CLS diag) | 31.7% | +13.3pp | 0.031*\n        C (oracle diag) | 40.0% | +21.7pp | 0.004**\n      - |\n        Table: Re-Repair pass@5 Comparison\n        A1: 28.3% → B: 43.3% → C: 53.3%\n        CLS-diagnostic nearly halves the gap between no-info and oracle\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with 95% CI error bars: resolve rate by condition. Clear monotonic gradient D < A1 < A2 < B < C.\"\n      - \"Paired instance analysis: heatmap showing which instances flip from unresolved→resolved with diagnostic info. Concentration in multi-test-failure instances.\"\n    analysis: |\n      Re-repair 结果强力支持 downstream utility claim。核心 insight：\n      1. CLS diagnostic info 即使有 ~12% error rate 仍提供 +13pp resolve rate 提升\n      2. 提升集中在 multi-test-failure instances（与 oracle-f2p-stratified 结果一致：T2+ instances 贡献 >80% of improvement）\n      3. 清晰梯度证明 diagnostic quality matters（random hurts, noisy-but-real helps, perfect helps most）\n      4. Oracle-CLS gap (8pp) 量化了 verifier 改进的剩余空间，motivating future work\n      \n      这直接回应 reviewer concern \"no downstream utility\"：per-test diagnostic 不仅在 accuracy 上 equivalent to trajectory-level，还 enables a concrete downstream application。\n\n  - name: swebench-pertest-data\n    plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n    description: \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test ground-truth labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances: 500\n      candidates_per_instance: 16\n      total_evaluations: 8000\n      successful_docker_runs: 7680\n      docker_failure_rate: 0.04\n      mean_tests_per_instance: 12.3\n      median_tests_per_instance: 8\n      f2p_distribution:\n        T1_pct: 45.2\n        T2_pct: 22.8\n        T3_5_pct: 18.6\n        T6plus_pct: 13.4\n      mean_resolve_rate_across_candidates: 0.31\n      total_per_test_labels: 94720\n      wall_time_hours: 18\n      parallelism: 16\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench Verified 有 500 个 curated instances。每个 instance 跑 16 个 repair candidate（来自不同 repair agent/model 的 patches）。Docker evaluation 的 failure rate 约 4%（timeout, dependency issues）。\n      \n      F2P test distribution 比 func-level dataset 更丰富（mean 12.3 vs func-level 的 2.3），因为 repo-level tests 涵盖更多 edge cases。T6+ 占 13.4% 意味着 per-test granularity 的优势在 repo-level 更大。\n      \n      这个 dataset 是 resource contribution：first large-scale per-test labeled dataset for SWE-bench。支撑 repo-level training 和 re-repair evaluation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\n        Instances: 500 | Candidates/instance: 16 | Total evaluations: 8000\n        Successful runs: 7680 (96%) | Total per-test labels: 94,720\n        Mean tests/instance: 12.3 | Median: 8\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of tests-per-instance distribution, showing long tail (some instances with 50+ tests)\"\n    analysis: \"Dataset 构建成功，为 repo-level experiments 和 re-repair evaluation 提供基础。F2P distribution 比 func-level 更重 tail（T6+ 13.4% vs 5.1%），预示 per-test advantage 在 repo-level 更显著。\"\n\n  - name: diagnostic-rerepair-pilot\n    plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n    description: \"Original planned experiment: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs no info on 200 instances. Superseded by re-repair-phase1-instruct design but kept for completeness.\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 200\n      control_resolve_rate: 0.19\n      cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.33\n      delta_pp: 14.0\n      paired_t_p_value: 0.008\n      effect_size_cohens_d: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"在 200 instances 上 paired design 给出更强 statistical power。Delta 14pp 在 best tier [10,18] 范围内。Larger n 使得 p < 0.01 成为可能。Effect size medium (d=0.42) 反映 diagnostic info 是 useful-but-not-transformative intervention。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Larger sample 版本确认 re-repair-phase1-instruct 的发现，提供更强 statistical evidence。\"\n\n  # === Composite Analysis for Paper ===\n  - name: deepseek-repo-composite-analysis\n    plan_id: repo-level-training\n    description: \"Cross-model repo-level comparison: Qwen vs DeepSeek × CLS vs CWM. Design space characterization 的核心 table。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Qwen3-4B repo-level (from existing data)\n      qwen4b_cls_accuracy: 83.63\n      qwen4b_cwm_accuracy: 58.04\n      qwen4b_cwm_unparseable_pct: 53.7\n      qwen4b_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 25.59\n      # Qwen3-8B repo-level (from existing data)\n      qwen8b_cls_accuracy: 84.79\n      qwen8b_cwm_unparseable_pct: 93.0\n      # DeepSeek repo-level (predicted)\n      deepseek_cls_accuracy: 81.6\n      deepseek_cwm_accuracy: 77.7\n      deepseek_cwm_unparseable_pct: 13.0\n      deepseek_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 3.9\n      # DeepSeek func-level (from existing data)\n      deepseek_func_cls_accuracy: 86.85\n      deepseek_func_cwm_accuracy: 86.83\n      deepseek_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 0.02\n      # Qwen func-level (from existing data)\n      qwen_func_cls_accuracy: 88.41\n      qwen_func_cwm_accuracy: 87.19\n      qwen_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp: 1.22\n      # TRAJ comparison\n      deepseek_traj_repo_accuracy: 77.1\n      qwen_traj_repo_accuracy: 85.66\n    result_rationale: |\n      Design space characterization 的核心 evidence：\n      \n      Function-level: CLS ≈ CWM 在两个 model family 上都成立（gap < 1.5pp，TOST equivalence confirmed）。证明 formulation choice at low complexity 不重要。\n      \n      Repo-level divergence pattern:\n      - Qwen: CLS >> CWM (25pp gap)，因为 CWM unparseable 53-93%。Tokenizer 无法 handle structured multi-test output。\n      - DeepSeek: CLS > CWM (4pp gap)，CWM unparseable 仅 13%。Tokenizer 支持 structured generation。\n      \n      这是 Path B narrative：formulation advantage magnitude is model-contingent。CLS 仍有 consistent（小）优势，但 CWM 在合适的 tokenizer 下 functional。\n      \n      关键 insight：Qwen 的 CWM \"failure\" 不是因为 generation-based verification 不可行，而是因为其 tokenizer 在长结构化输出时 degenerate。DeepSeek 证明这不是 formulation-inherent limitation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Design Space — Accuracy by Formulation × Model × Complexity\n                    | Function-Level      | Repo-Level\n        Model       | CLS   | CWM  | Gap  | CLS   | CWM   | Gap   | CWM Unparse\n        Qwen3-4B    | 88.4  | 87.2 | +1.2 | 83.6  | 58.0  | +25.6 | 53.7%\n        Qwen3-8B    | 90.5  | 87.7 | +2.8 | 84.8  | —     | —     | 93.0%\n        DeepSeek-8B | 86.9  | 86.8 | +0.0 | 81.6  | 77.7  | +3.9  | 13.0%\n      - |\n        Table: Formulation Robustness Summary\n        Formulation | Func-Level (2 models) | Repo-Level (2 models)\n        CLS         | 86.9–90.5 (robust)    | 81.6–84.8 (robust)\n        CWM         | 86.8–87.7 (robust)    | 58.0–77.7 (fragile, model-dependent)\n        TRAJ        | 85.7–86.2             | 77.1–85.7 (variable)\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap: rows = model family (Qwen, DeepSeek), cols = complexity (func, repo). Cell color = CLS-CWM gap. Shows divergence only in top-right (Qwen × repo).\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: CWM unparseable rate (x) vs CLS-CWM accuracy gap (y). Strong positive correlation. Qwen repo as outlier, DeepSeek repo near origin.\"\n    analysis: |\n      Best tier narrative 完全成立：\n      1. Claim 1 (equivalence at func-level): ✓ 两个 model family 均 confirmed\n      2. Claim 2 (model-contingent divergence): ✓ DeepSeek CWM functional (13% unparse) vs Qwen CWM collapse (53-93%)\n      3. Claim 3 (diagnostic granularity): ✓ CLS per-test matches TRAJ accuracy while enabling re-repair\n      4. Claim 4 (downstream utility): ✓ +13pp resolve rate from CLS diagnostic info\n      \n      EMNLP Main 投稿强度：4 个 clean contributions，controlled comparison methodology，两个 model families 交叉验证，downstream application validated。唯一 limitation 是 repo-level sample size 较小（48 test instances per seed），但 multi-seed replication 部分弥补。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"af9104f1-6ad4-4926-a0cf-0c7bcf3666b7","total_cost_usd":0.4274205000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33520,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":7361,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33520,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7361,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33520},"type":"message"}],"